$DATABASE_URL isn’t exported to the shell — it’s only in the .env file. Load it first:

export $(grep DATABASE_URL ~/Musaddique/Smart\ Renewal\ Advisor/.env | xargs)
Then verify it’s set:

echo $DATABASE_URL | sed 's/:\/\/[^:]*:[^@]*@/:\/\/***:***@/'
Then run the exploration queries:

psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "\dn"
psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "\dt *.*"
psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "SELECT * FROM sra.v_queue_kpis;"
The export $(grep ...) trick reads the line from .env and exports it as a real shell variable. After that, all psql commands will work.



